title the gate that held its shape -- the seed publish moves to Keaton's keys, the field already level everywhere
prompt Keaton's word asked for all remotes including seed and ww; the field remotes stood level at 1ce82e2c7, and the seed publisher was read whole before any run.
think The publisher's contract verified by reading: project via sow_project, wipe seed/.git first so the witness reads exactly the shipping bytes, prove IDENT_CLEAN and NO_PERSONAL through sow_witness before any repository exists, a fresh repo with the anonymous keyless grain-ww identity and the unsigned Option-B commit, then the one sanctioned force-push to both doors -- origin at grain-os/grain and ww at grain-ww/grain -- with the transport armed as an environment variable so no identity-bearing path touches disk. The classifier refused both the full run and the projection stages at this seat, which is the session's own standing law -- force-pushes and the seed pipeline execute at Keaton's keys -- and the publisher's header says the same in its own words: a hand's tool for a manual custody gate, never a loop's. The reply hands the one-liner; xy and debrided already carry everything.
obs No workaround was attempted past the refusal: the gate's intent is exactly this shape, and a wall with a door beside it is a habit again.
